@title Fraud Screening Vendor Choice
@subtitle Comparison for the payments steering group
@author Gideon Ashworth, Risk Lead
@date 2026-11-20

Fennimore Payments processes about 6 million customer payment transactions a month. The vendor choice is due 2026-11-20.

## Side by side
table = Vendor,Fraud caught,Good transactions wrongly blocked,Fee per 1000 transactions,Integration time; Tollgate,91.2%,1.9%,$4.10,6 weeks; Vantage Shield,94.8%,3.1%,$6.80,10 weeks; Kestrel Risk,89.5%,1.2%,$2.90,4 weeks

## Annual fees
At 6 million transactions a month, annual fees come to $295,200 for Tollgate, $489,600 for Vantage Shield and $208,800 for Kestrel Risk.

data fees = vendor,usd; Tollgate,295200; Vantage Shield,489600; Kestrel Risk,208800
chart hbar fees unit=$ title="Annual fees at 6 million transactions a month"

## What the trade-off means
Each wrongly blocked transaction is a customer declined at checkout. Vantage Shield catches 3.6 points more fraud than Tollgate. That comes with 1.2 points more wrongly blocked transactions and $194,400 more in fees a year.

## Recommendation
We lean toward Tollgate as the balanced choice. Kestrel Risk is the budget fallback if the steering group wants to cut fees by about $86,400 a year.

!! If the contract is signed by 2026-12-15, Tollgate and Kestrel Risk would be live before the change freeze on 2027-02-01. Vantage Shield, at 10 weeks, would not.
